    "body": "## Summary\n- expose requester-friendly assignment choices on job creation: “Kto pierwszy, ten bierze” (`INSTANT`) or “Chcę wybrać wykonawcę” (`PROPOSALS`)\n- keep price negotiation as a separate opt-in available only in proposal mode\n- explain the initial escrow hold and higher/lower accepted-proposal adjustment before publication\n- add private proposal API client operations and a dedicated job-details proposal panel\n- let workers submit only their own proposal, with no competitor offer visibility\n- hide price input entirely for fixed-price proposal jobs\n- let requesters review candidates with public trust cards, amount and private message, then choose one\n- update the UI immediately after selection so the winner is accepted and remaining submitted proposals are marked rejected\n- prevent discovery cards and job details from presenting the legacy direct-accept action for proposal-mode jobs\n- surface assignment mode / negotiation semantics on discovery cards and job details\n- document the complete web privacy and escrow experience\n\n## Product behavior\nSimple errands remain one-click `INSTANT` jobs. `PROPOSALS` is opt-in and does not automatically mean bidding: requesters may select a person while keeping the price fixed. Negotiation is a separate checkbox.\n\n## Privacy\nThe frontend never fetches a global/public proposal feed. It calls the authenticated job proposal endpoint whose server contract returns all proposals only to the requester and only the caller’s proposal to another user. Exact job locations, live tracking, wallet/payment data, verification documents and moderation data are not added to this UI.\n\n## Escrow\nThe create form states that the published amount is held immediately. For negotiable jobs it explains that a higher accepted offer requires the missing delta before assignment and a lower offer refunds the excess. The frontend does not perform wallet math; the backend remains authoritative and atomic.\n\n## Validation\nRun production dependency audit, ESLint, Vite build, backend Maven verify and repository runtime smoke. Do not merge unless the latest head is fully green.",
